* mx-m1-currentreuse: current-reuse ACTIVE-LOAD gate-pumped down-mixer.
* Lineage: current-reuse / bleeding mixer archetype (single-ended IF), e.g.
* resistive-feedback current-reuse mixer with active load. Motivation: mx-a1's
* PASSIVE drain load gives conversion LOSS; a PMOS current-reuse active load
* (PM1) presents high impedance at the IF and reuses the bias current -> IF
* voltage GAIN, single-ended IF. Structure-only, ZERO component values.
* Harness convention: RF in = VIN1 (portnum 1), IF out = VOUT1 (portnum 2),
* LO net = VLO (harness single-ended large-signal drive). RF+LO sum at the NM1
* gate (n1); NM1 drain = IF node n2; PM1 (VDD active load) drain = n2; a
* trans-impedance feedback R (Rfb n2->n1) sets the TIA gain; IF DC-blocked (C2)
* to VOUT1. Published in-topology BIAS: NMOS mirror ref (R1->diode NM2) feeds
* the NM1 gate via R2; PMOS load mirror ref (R3->diode PM2 from VDD) sets PM1
* gate n3. V1.1 achievability candidate (approved 2026-09-17), NOT yet an anchor.
C C1 VIN1 n0
L L1 n0 n1
NMOS NM1 n2 n1 VSS VSS
C Clo VLO n1
PMOS PM1 n2 n3 VDD VDD
R Rfb n2 n1
C C2 n2 VOUT1
R R1 VDD n4
NMOS NM2 n4 n4 VSS VSS
R R2 n4 n1
R R3 VSS n3
PMOS PM2 n3 n3 VDD VDD
